Change only the members named. An empty value clears one, as in --model "". The result is checked as a whole profile.

--key reads a new key as create does, into the OS keychain, or into profiles.json with --file. --provider keeps base_url, account_id and model, and names on stderr the ones it keeps. On a profile that holds a key it needs --key, since a key belongs to one provider. An account_id kept on a provider that takes none is refused, so clear it with --account-id "" in the same update. There is no rename. Delete the profile and create it again.

Usage:
  onesie profile update NAME [flags]

Examples:
  onesie profile update work --model typesafe/jev-1.13
  pass show work | head -n 1 | onesie profile update work --key

Flags:
      --account-id string   cloudflare only, the account id, 32 hexadecimal characters
      --allow-http          store a plain http --base-url to a host other than this machine. Every run on the profile then needs --allow-http too
      --base-url string     the api root the profile's runs use
      --file                with --key, store the new key in profiles.json, not the OS keychain
  -h, --help                help for update
      --key                 read a new key from a prompt or stdin
      --model string        the model a run uses when it names none
      --provider string     a new provider for the profile. On a profile that holds a key it needs --key

Global Flags:
      --profile string   the profile a run uses, from profiles.json in the config dir. Overrides ONESIE_PROFILE and ONESIE_PROVIDER, and otherwise the default profile runs, which onesie profile use sets
